  "description": "The ExcelsiusGPS is a robotic navigation and trajectory alignment platform developed by Globus Medical (originating from Excelsius Surgical, acquired in 2014) for open and minimally invasive spine surgery and stereotactic cranial neurosurgery. The system consists of a floor-mounted mobile base with a rigid serial robotic arm and a separate optical navigation camera cart that tracks a dynamic reference array alongside an independent surveillance marker to detect patient registration shift. Compatible with preoperative CT/MRI, intraoperative 3D CT/CBCT (including Excelsius3D), and 2D fluoroscopy workflows, the robotic arm positions a rigid guide tube along planned trajectories for pedicle screw insertion, interbody cage preparation, or cranial electrode/biopsy placement while an integrated end-effector force sensor monitors lateral tool deflection (skiving). The platform received CE mark certification and US FDA 510(k) clearance for spine procedures in 2017 and for cranial neurosurgery in 2020.",
